    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Yordan Alvarez** (76.89) and **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (74.82) anchoring the offense as our clear top plays. **Yordan Alvarez** benefits from an elite xwOBA of .450 against Tanner Bibee, while **Pete Crow-Armstrong** is a strategic must-start; beyond his solid projection, the matchup against Kevin Gausman offers a +4% boost due to a favorable SB environment, reinforcing our mandate to prioritize elite speed. Further down the order, **Colt Keith** (69.64) provides our highest value outside the outfield, capitalizing on a soft matchup against Erick Fedde, where a combination of park factors and the +19% SP skill advantage allows him to outperform his base projection significantly.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was leaving **Casey Schmitt** (44.05) out of the active roster. While his projection sat within a point of **Kazuma Okamoto** (44.35), the optimizer ultimately favored **Kazuma Okamoto** due to his slightly superior park factor, despite his struggles against Ben Brown. We are also closely monitoring the lineup for **Chase Meidroth**, who draws the toughest assignment of the day against Tarik Skubal. While his 49.98 score is buoyed by a +10% order bonus for the leadoff spot, the -19% penalty for facing Skubal creates a high-variance profile that warrants close attention once official lineups are posted.\n\nRisks remain elevated across the board as every single slot remains in \"Lineup Pending\" status. While we have projected **Dillon Dingler** and **Josh Smith** based on their typical spots, any shift in the batting order could immediately degrade their efficiency scores. Managers should also note that **Luke Raley** (38.28) was considered for his SB utility, but his matchup against Ranger Suarez resulted in a sub-40 efficiency score, keeping him on the bench to preserve our game caps. We are proceeding with this configuration, relying on the speed upside of **Pete Crow-Armstrong** and **Caleb Durbin** to keep our stolen base category competitive despite a challenging day of opposing arms.",
